ous activity; high: &#x02265;20 minutes of vigorous activity.</p></fn><fn id="T2FN6"><label>f</label><p>Underweight = BMI (kg/m<sup>2</sup>) &#x0003c;18.5; normal weight = BMI 18.5-24.9; overweight = BMI 25.0-29.9; obese = BMI &#x02265;30.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Age-Adjusted Prevalence<xref rid="T3FN1" ref-type="table-fn">a</xref> of Self-reported Diagnosed Diseases and Conditions for Non-Hispanic Black and Non-Hispanic White Respondents (N = 56,754) to the Adventist Health Study-2, by Sex, Preliminary Analysis, United States, 2001&#x02013;2005</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" scope="col" rowspan="3" colspan="1">Disease or Condition</th><th align="center" scope="col" colspan="3" rowspan="1">Non-Hispanic Black (N = 14,376)</th><th align="center" scope="col" colspan="3" rowspan="1">Non-Hispanic White (N= 42,378)</th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="3" colspan="1"><bold><italic>P</italic> value<xref rid="T3FN2" ref-type="table-fn">b</xref></bold></th></tr><tr><th colspan="6" rowspan="1"><hr/></th></tr><tr><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Male No. (%)</th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Female No. (%)</th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Total No. (%)</th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Male No. (%)</th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Female No. (%)</th><th align="center" scope="col" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Total No. (%)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" scope="row" rowspan="1" colspan="1">High blood pressure</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1325 (31.9)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3,392 (34.3)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">4,717 (33.6)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">3,814 (25.0)</td><td align="right" rowspan="1" colspan="1">6,854 (26.0)</td><td align=